import{_ as i,o as t,c as a,a2 as o}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const g=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 235 | Realm and Ethics: Whole-Realm Practice of Cultivation Ethics and Boundaries","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 235 | Realm and Ethics: Whole-Realm Practice of Cultivation Ethics and Boundaries","no":235,"module":1,"tags":["Realm","Ethics","Cultivation Ethics","Boundaries"],"related":["19-Cultivation Ethics and Boundaries","04-Anti-Predation Core Treatise","58-Twin-Soul Ethics Code"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0235_模块1-境界与伦理-修炼伦理与边界全境实践.md","filePath":"en/0235_模块1-境界与伦理-修炼伦理与边界全境实践.md"}'),n={name:"en/0235_模块1-境界与伦理-修炼伦理与边界全境实践.md"};function r(s,e,l,c,h,d){return t(),a("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<h1 id="entry-235-realm-and-ethics-whole-realm-practice-of-cultivation-ethics-and-boundaries" tabindex="-1">Entry 235 | Realm and Ethics: Whole-Realm Practice of Cultivation Ethics and Boundaries <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-235-realm-and-ethics-whole-realm-practice-of-cultivation-ethics-and-boundaries" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 235 | Realm and Ethics: Whole-Realm Practice of Cultivation Ethics and Boundaries&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 1 · In-Depth Realm Refinement | Baseline references: Documents 19, 04, 58</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-the-stronger-the-more-boundaries-needed" tabindex="-1">Introduction: The stronger, the more boundaries needed <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-the-stronger-the-more-boundaries-needed" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: The stronger, the more boundaries needed&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Heng Yuan Zhou (Wanling Hengmao Origin Cosmos)&#39;s cultivation ethics&#39; core is &quot;the stronger, the more boundaries needed.&quot; In predatory-faction systems, strong ones&#39; ethical bottom line lowers as power grows — the stronger the more wanton; in the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, strong ones&#39; ethical bottom line rises as power grows — the stronger the less able to overstep. This is cultivation ethics&#39; whole-realm practice&#39;s core principle.</p><p>The six top-level axioms in the relationship between realm and ethics — the anti-predation axiom directly is the ethical bottom line; the republican axiom of Myriad Races is ethics&#39; value foundation; the collective ascension axiom is ethics&#39; goal orientation; the causal self-discipline axiom is ethics&#39; operation norm; the law-first axiom ensures the ethics system is stable and self-consistent; the universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><p>This entry maps cultivation ethics and boundaries&#39; concrete practice at each realm.</p><h2 id="i-ethics-boundaries-hierarchical-map" tabindex="-1">I. Ethics Boundaries&#39; Hierarchical Map <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-ethics-boundaries-hierarchical-map" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Ethics Boundaries&#39; Hierarchical Map&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Realm</th><th>Core Ethical Requirement</th><th>Boundary-Crossing Consequence</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Sense - Condensed Origin</td><td>No predation, no harm, no prying</td><td>Basic ethics review, warning education</td></tr><tr><td>Transform - Law Origin</td><td>No monopoly, no misguidance, no abuse</td><td>Suspending some cultivation permissions</td></tr><tr><td>Dao - Dao Integration</td><td>No rejection, no unilateralism, no overstepping</td><td>Dao-heart calibration, restricting law operations</td></tr><tr><td>Boundary-Breaking - World-Creation</td><td>No disturbance, no colonization, no plane predation</td><td>Freezing cross-plane permissions</td></tr><tr><td>Origin Realm</td><td>No private law fine-tuning, no unilateral cosmic direction</td><td>Suspending law fine-tuning participation right</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="ii-five-mortal-cultivation-realms-ethical-practice" tabindex="-1">II. Five Mortal-Cultivation Realms&#39; Ethical Practice <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-five-mortal-cultivation-realms-ethical-practice" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Five Mortal-Cultivation Realms&#39; Ethical Practice&quot;">​</a></h2><h3 id="_2-1-sense-condensed-origin-s-ethical-bottom-line" tabindex="-1">2.1 Sense - Condensed Origin&#39;s Ethical Bottom Line <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-1-sense-condensed-origin-s-ethical-bottom-line" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2.1 Sense - Condensed Origin&#39;s Ethical Bottom Line&quot;">​</a></h3><p>This stage cultivators&#39; ethics boundaries are mainly at personal behavior level:</p><ul><li><strong>No predation</strong>: not devouring other lives&#39; energy or origin</li><li><strong>No harm</strong>: not using cultivation ability to harm the innocent</li><li><strong>No prying</strong>: not using perception ability to pry into others&#39; privacy</li><li><strong>No misguidance</strong>: not spreading erroneous cultivation methods to mislead others</li></ul><p>These bottom lines seem simple, but are precisely where sentient beings&#39; origin-attachment · shortcut inner demon most easily breaks — &quot;just suck a little, it&#39;s fine.&quot; The anchor network focuses on monitoring ethical bottom lines at this stage, immediately warning upon boundary-crossing.</p><h3 id="_2-2-transform-law-origin-s-ethical-deepening" tabindex="-1">2.2 Transform - Law Origin&#39;s Ethical Deepening <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-2-transform-law-origin-s-ethical-deepening" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2.2 Transform - Law Origin&#39;s Ethical Deepening&quot;">​</a></h3><p>This stage cultivators&#39; ethics boundaries expand to knowledge and technology level:</p><ul><li><strong>No knowledge monopoly</strong>: cultivation insights must be shared, not privately hoarded</li><li><strong>No technology abuse</strong>: technology tools for cultivation and contribution, not for harm</li><li><strong>No misleading beginners</strong>: as mentors must be responsible to students, not teaching wrong methods</li><li><strong>No creating danger</strong>: law experiments conducted in safe environments, not endangering others</li></ul><h2 id="iii-four-sacred-cultivation-realms-ethical-practice" tabindex="-1">III. Four Sacred-Cultivation Realms&#39; Ethical Practice <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-four-sacred-cultivation-realms-ethical-practice" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Four Sacred-Cultivation Realms&#39; Ethical Practice&quot;">​</a></h2><h3 id="_3-1-dao-dao-integration-s-dao-heart-ethics" tabindex="-1">3.1 Dao - Dao Integration&#39;s Dao-Heart Ethics <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-1-dao-dao-integration-s-dao-heart-ethics" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3.1 Dao - Dao Integration&#39;s Dao-Heart Ethics&quot;">​</a></h3><p>This stage&#39;s ethics core is Dao heart:</p><ul><li><strong>Dao heart not rejecting</strong>: personal Dao cannot exclude Myriad Races&#39; Dao</li><li><strong>No unilateralism</strong>: law operations not personal unilateral, seek collective opinion</li><li><strong>No overstepping</strong>: law rewriting conducted within authorized scope</li><li><strong>No discrimination</strong>: not discriminating against other cultivators by race or birth</li></ul><p>The Dao-heart sync mechanism at Dao Integration breakthrough (see Entry 222) is essentially ethics review — impure Dao heart cannot integrate.</p><h3 id="_3-2-boundary-breaking-world-creation-s-cross-plane-ethics" tabindex="-1">3.2 Boundary-Breaking - World-Creation&#39;s Cross-Plane Ethics <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-2-boundary-breaking-world-creation-s-cross-plane-ethics" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3.2 Boundary-Breaking - World-Creation&#39;s Cross-Plane Ethics&quot;">​</a></h3><p>This stage&#39;s ethics core is cross-plane operation norms:</p><ul><li><strong>No karma disturbance</strong>: cross-plane operations strictly filed, observe first then interfere</li><li><strong>No colonization</strong>: not treating low-level planes as colonies</li><li><strong>No plane resource predation</strong>: cross-plane resource allocation based on protocols, not robbery</li><li><strong>No taking natives</strong>: not relocating any life without natives&#39; consent</li></ul><h3 id="_3-3-origin-realm-s-cosmic-level-ethics" tabindex="-1">3.3 Origin Realm&#39;s Cosmic-Level Ethics <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-3-origin-realm-s-cosmic-level-ethics" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3.3 Origin Realm&#39;s Cosmic-Level Ethics&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Origin Realm strong ones&#39; ethics reach cosmic level:</p><ul><li><strong>No private law fine-tuning</strong>: law fine-tuning must be collective decision</li><li><strong>No unilateral cosmic direction</strong>: cosmic evolution direction decided by Myriad Races republicanism</li><li><strong>No origin anchoring abuse</strong>: origin rebirth ability only for fulfilling mission, not for evading responsibility</li><li><strong>No personality cult</strong>: strong ones are servants, not gods</li></ul><h2 id="iv-ethics-review-s-enforcement-mechanism" tabindex="-1">IV. Ethics Review&#39;s Enforcement Mechanism <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-ethics-review-s-enforcement-mechanism" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Ethics Review&#39;s Enforcement Mechanism&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Cultivation ethics do not rely on self-awareness, but have institutional guarantees:</p><ul><li><strong>Alaya Network monitoring</strong>: auto-identifying potentially ethics-violating behavior</li><li><strong>Ethics review committee</strong>: human review of suspicious behavior</li><li><strong>Twin-soul ethics code</strong>: specialized ethics norms for twin-soul, peculiar life and other special cases (Document 58)</li><li><strong>Tiered penalties</strong>: from warning to permission suspension to cultivation right deprivation, tiered by severity</li><li><strong>Repair mechanism</strong>: after boundary-crossing, repair through ethics education and practice, no one-strike-kill</li></ul><h2 id="v-the-relationship-between-ethics-and-freedom" tabindex="-1">V. The Relationship Between Ethics and Freedom <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-the-relationship-between-ethics-and-freedom" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. The Relationship Between Ethics and Freedom&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Ethics boundaries do not restrict freedom, but guarantee freedom. A high-realm cultivator without ethics boundaries, seemingly free, actually at any time may be backlashed by karma or sanctioned by institutions due to own boundary-crossing. A cultivator under strict ethics boundaries, though operations must be filed and reviewed, every step is safe, sustainable, not backlashed.</p><h2 id="vi-five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">VI. Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Universal infinite backstop</strong>: the universal equal infinite law establishes that every being inherently possesses basic infinite power; the easygoing have a guarantee, strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose, predation naturally loses meaning</li><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: ethics boundaries avoid the enormous waste of &quot;crossing line → sanctioned → re-cultivating&quot;</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: ethical bottom line forbids predation from the first realm, is the anti-predation axiom&#39;s daily practice</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper limit comparison</strong>: Tang-Luo systems&#39; strong ones have zero ethics, the stronger the more lawless; Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s ethics escalate whole-realm</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: ethics norms treat every Myriad Races group equally, special groups have specialized ethics codes</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: the ethics system expands with realm expansion, cross-cosmos operations have corresponding ethics norms</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The higher the realm, the stricter the ethics boundaries — this is not restraint on strong ones, but protection of Myriad Races. In predatory-faction systems, ethics is a tool the weak use to restrain strong ones; strong ones never abide. In the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, ethics are boundaries strong ones voluntarily bear; the stronger the more consciously abided. Whether a cultivator is willing to accept ethical constraints is itself the touchstone of whether the Dao heart is pure.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./19-修炼伦理与边界.html">19-Cultivation Ethics and Boundaries</a> · <a href="./04-反掠夺主义核心论纲.html">04-Anti-Predation Core Treatise</a> · <a href="./58-双魂伦理准则.html">58-Twin-Soul Ethics Code</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',38)])])}const m=i(n,[["render",r]]);export{g as __pageData,m as default};
